<div class="<%= layout_framework_classes %>">
  <div class="<%= layout_framework_title_classes %>">
    <%= render 'framework/page_header', page_name: :paint_colors %>
  </div>

  <div class="<%= layout_framework_content_classes %>">
    <%= render_framework_intro_paragraph(:paint_colors) %>

    <div class="space-y-16">
      <section class="space-y-8">
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <%= framework_heading(3, 'Color and token fills') %>
          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %>">
            Every function takes an optional <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">{ el }</code>: the id
            or element whose nearest <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">.screen</code>
            supplies the paint. Each returns a
            <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">Fill</code>; the shape and how the reading works
            are on <%= render DocsRef.new(page: :paint_api) %>.
          </p>
          <ul class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %> list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
            <li>
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">bg(token, { el })</code>: a background token
              (<code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">bg--&lt;token&gt;</code>), e.g.
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">'black'</code>,
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">'gray-40'</code>,
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">'red-55'</code>. On solid modes you get a color-only
              Fill; on dither modes, a pattern Fill.
            </li>
            <li>
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">text(token, { el })</code>: a text token
              (<code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">text--&lt;token&gt;</code>). Framework text is painted by
              clipping a background to the letters, so the Fill carries both the color and the image.
            </li>
            <li>
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">stroke(token, { el })</code>: a stroke token
              (<code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">text-stroke--&lt;token&gt;</code>), returned as a
              concrete <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">rgb</code> in a color-only Fill.
            </li>
            <li>
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">semantic(slot, { el })</code>: a framework semantic
              slot. Slots with a public utility (<code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">canvas</code>,
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">surface</code>,
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">text-primary</code>,
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">text-secondary</code>,
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">text-inverse</code>,
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">backdrop</code>) are read through that utility.
              The rest (<code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">border-strong</code>,
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">border-muted</code>,
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">fill-strong</code>,
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">fill-muted</code>,
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">fill-soft</code>,
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">stroke-contrast</code>,
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">icon</code>) are read from their
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">--framework-semantic-*</code> variables,
              patterns included.
            </li>
            <li>
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">textColor(token, { el })</code>: the single
              color of a named text utility
              (<code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">'default'</code>,
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">'muted'</code>, ...), for SVG or canvas text.
              When the text is painted with a pattern, you get the pattern's ink, the color the letters actually
              read as.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-4">
          <%= render CodeExampleComponent.new(demo_code: '// Resolve a token for the current screen mode/theme.
var fill = TRMNLPaint.bg("red-55", { el: "my-chart" });
// => solid mode:  { color: "rgb(204, 0, 0)", image: null, url: null, size: null }
// => dither mode: { color: "rgb(255,255,255)", image: "url(...)", url: "data:...", size: 16 }

// One-color form of the semantic default text utility for SVG/canvas text.
var textColor = TRMNLPaint.textColor("default", { el: "my-chart" });', language: 'javascript') %>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-8">
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <%= framework_heading(3, 'Painting fills') %>
          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %>">
            A resolved Fill is painted back with one call. Wrap paints in
            <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">watch()</code> so they re-run when the screen's mode,
            dark or theme classes change; see <%= render DocsRef.new(page: :paint_api) %>.
          </p>
          <ul class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %> list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
            <li>
              <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">apply(node, fill)</code>: paints a node's background
              from a Fill, layering the color under the pattern exactly as the framework itself does.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-4">
          <%= render CodeExampleComponent.new(demo_code: 'var swatch = document.getElementById("legend-swatch");

TRMNLPaint.watch(swatch, function () {
  // Solid on 4-bit+ panels, a composited dither tile on 1- and 2-bit screens.
  TRMNLPaint.apply(swatch, TRMNLPaint.bg("gray-30", { el: swatch }));
});', language: 'javascript') %>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>

    <%= render 'framework/page_navigation' %>
  </div>
</div>
